owing sounds of  Keats cries of Terror increased  attention immensely the jump scare that  comes from Keith suddenly waking up  delivers a perfect jolt to viewers and  acts as a great end Stinger to a scary  sequence it all ends with some good  laughs for the awkward exchange between  Tess and Keith but it's an unforgettably  tense moment early in the film that sets  the tone perfectly and instills some  good chills  even though we know that AJ is basically  the worst person ever as it becomes  clear that he's guilty of sexual assault  Tess doesn't know that and does  everything in her power to try and save  him after Tess initially escapes she  goes back into the house to Traverse the  dark corridors and eventually makes her  way back to the mother's room soon after  she notices a light peeking out through  the darkness and with one little  response she finds herself on the ground  with a bullet in her gut what Tess  didn't realize is that AJ was able to  get a pistol from Frank and is now  nervously going through the tunnel still  believing that the mother is hiding  somewhere thus when he sees a shadowy  figure standing just a short distance  away he doesn't hesitate to fire only  after he fires does he learn it was test  standing there the entire sequence is  thrilling the build-up to test returning  into the house is incredibly tense and  the moment she sees the light of AJ's  phone leaves you silent and then  instantly frightened by the well-timed  jump scare of The Gunshot you're left  even more scared afterward as Tess  clings on as she bleeds for the rest of  the film  just as all hope seems lost for tests  after the cops don't believe her and  she's once again left on her own she  decides to take the mother head-on with  the help of something mentioned by Andre  amongst his ramblings Andre mentions  that the mother only comes out at night  and with that knowledge Tess manages to  Ram her car into the mother when she  appears pinning her against the house  